Calc: an xlsx import under LOK waits without yielding

importSheetFragments parses sheets on pool threads and meanwhile runs
Application::Yield on the main thread. Under LOK a yield runs the
client's queued requests. When Calc's idle interprets a formula whose
external source is an xlsx (the hidden copy loads inside Interpret),
a request that reads that formula during the import finds it running
and gets Err:522, a circular reference. Seen on macOS, where any yield
drains the worker's requests: a cell read 1 s after a reader loads
returns Err:522 while the source imports.
Under LOK there is no window to keep painting: release the solar mutex
and wait for the sheet threads; the yield loop then finds none left.
Desktop builds still yield.

diff --git a/sc/source/filter/oox/workbookfragment.cxx b/sc/source/filter/oox/workbookfragment.cxx
